  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Output 1: Clean energy and drinking water supply feasibility studies, and engineering designs completed, bidding documents prepared, and implementation contracts procured. The PRF will conduct all necessary demand assessments, clean energy resource assessments, geotechnical mapping and investigations, climate projections, complete safeguards assessments including surveys and consultations and cumulative assessments to develop an optimal engineering design with emphasis on climate and disaster resilience, and gender inclusive development for the identified priority projects. The PRF will also undertake strategic procurement planning and market analyses for the ensuing projects, prepare bidding documents and support the bid process to procure implementation contracts. It will also determine an integrated approach to bundle smaller projects and effectively resource these investments The PRF will also determine the suitable procurement approach including the feasibility of the PPP modality, business structures, shareholding patterns, financial, management and operational plans for the proposed priority investments.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Output 2: Innovative and transformative energy solutions in the FSM piloted. The PRF will review and undertake small-scale pilot testing of innovative clean energy technologies, including (a) off the shelf scalable hydro solutions to demonstrate climate-resilient and low safeguard impact power production; (b) clean energy powered drinking water solutions for remote communities that are subjected to climate and disaster risks including increasing droughts and seawater surges that impact groundwater availability and potability and; (c)support other innovative solutions including on energy efficiency and the use of clean energy for transport. The PRF will procure equipment and materials needed for the pilots. Appropriate arrangements for the proposed pilot-testing activities, including the site, permits for the activities, handover, and maintenance of assets financed under the PRF, will be agreed upon with the executing and implementing agency as part of project preparation. The pilots will be reviewed for scale-up under ensuing projects.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Output 3: Sector policies, investment strategies, and plans for improved energy transition updated. The PRF will provide inputs to update national and state investment plans including avenues to accelerate the deployment of clean energy to support FSM&amp;apos;s fossil fuel use reduction and climate change plans. This includes support for modeling reviews, state and national roadmaps for accelerated energy efficiency and clean energy and water supply adoption, preparation and adoption of codes, standards, and structuring arrangements, including for official and private co-financing.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 4</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Output 4: Capacity of executing and implementing agencies strengthened and implementation arrangements tested. The PRF will support project preparation, including household surveys and primary data collection, efficiently and effectively, to ensure that selected projects are planned, designed, and implemented in a coordinated and time-bound manner despite coronavirus disease (COVID-19) related challenges. Government, utilities, and community implementation capacity will be strengthened through deployments, certified training and support on hydropower, renewable energy, drinking water supply, energy efficiency, electric mobility, procurement, governance, financial management, safeguards assessment, climate change &amp; disaster risk assessments, community engagement, communications, and operations</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
